Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

It might seem natural to feel hopeless, or discouraged.

That's not what God wants us to feel, though! He wants us to be hopeful,
and encouraged!

The start of this week wasn't what I was hoping it would look like. There
are a lot of things that have been better than last week, so there's no
reason to surrender myself to the negative thoughts that would beguile me.
It has been frustrating not seeing a lot of change, however.

I trust that as I give my energy to do his will, I can be encouraged and
hopeful in any circumstance. I am going to try and guide my actions to be
in sync with what God would have me do, with an increased drive!

The week slowly passed by
Here=E2=80=99re some Interesting things that happened:

Went to Bishop's house for dinner, he shared an ancient family tradition
that ended with me having oil smeared all over my face =F0=9F=A4=A6=E2=80=
=8D=E2=99=82=EF=B8=8F

Stopped by an art store! I talked with a sweet lady inside, and when she
saw my church name tag she grabbed onto my arm and started telling me about
how she had visited America before! She was so sweet a d we need to go back
and visit her soon. She had a certain light about her. She also gave me a
discount when I bought a tube of paint =F0=9F=98=89

We were able to do an hour and a half of Housing at an apartment complex!
Doesn't sound like a huge feat but last week we did actually 0 hours of
finding so it was a big step! We didn't find anyone interested but there
were a few solid interactions =F0=9F=98=86

Picked up a selfie stick tripod thing for 300 yen from a Jimoty person.
Will invite them to our Eikaiwa through the website next time we are at the
church!

We had DCM this week too. It was Magbago=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=E2=80=99s first =
time leading one! I
think he did a great job. We had a fun Mogi and talked about the difference
between listening and hearing. I'm excited for our next DCM! He is wanting
to use me for a lot of it which sounds fun too. After DCM we went and ate
Ramen as a district. Was fun!

On Sunday we talked a lot after church with a member named Otani=E5=85=84=
=E5=BC=9F about
ice cream and art museum stuff. It was fun, and a nice way to spend part of
our Sunday.

We had a chance to eat at an Udon shop with one of our uninterested in
gospel friends. I don't think anyone has high hopes for him as far as
gospel stuff, but I think he's got great potential, and he wants to go eat
with us again!

It's time for that one random thing that's always in my emails: this time
I'm feeling Like a few haiku should hit the spot =F0=9F=98=8C

#1

=E2=80=9CLife is Meaningless,=E2=80=9D
Satan wouldst have you believe.
Ponder not those words.

#2

=E2=80=9CLove one another=E2=80=9D
Commanded our Redeemer.
=E2=80=9CTurn yourself outwards=E2=80=9D

#3

Clouds are mighty thin
You'd be surprised at just how
Close we are to God

#4

It's late, I will sleep.
I love all of you so much!
Elder Killian

